kc-tools: a kext's import binds by its declared libraries, not by where a bisection lands

SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT (this header and the added lines; kc-tools keeps its own licence)

link_kext() resolved every import with symtab_lookup(): one table of the kernel's exported names
and every earlier kext's, sorted by name (qsort, equal names in no defined order) and searched by
bisection. A name defined twice (IO80211Family's compat hz, m_gethdr, m_freem, microuptime, m_adj,
m_copydata ... are kernel names too) went to whichever copy the bisection landed on, and four
names added to the kernel moved four bindings (ext4, SFBwfm, SFAppleCIO). Now bind_lookup():
a pin (KC_BIND_PINS) first; one definition as before; then the importer's OSBundleLibraries;
then the kernel, the base; then one other kext, if one address remains. An import still
ambiguous, a pin that does not resolve, or a pin no import uses fails the build. Each import
with more than one definition is printed with its choice. Applies after kc-tools-arm64-text.patch.
UPSTREAM: yes (without the pins it is the plain rule).

